Every ShroudForge mod package needs a <code>mod.json</code> file in its root folder. ShroudForge reads it before preparing or starting the mod. It describes the package and the capabilities it requests.

== Required fields ==

The required fields are <code>id</code>, <code>name</code>, and <code>version</code>. Other fields are optional.

== Example ==

<pre>
{
  "$schema": "https://bonsaibauer.github.io/shroudforge/schemas/manifest.schema.json",
  "id": "example.hello-ember",
  "name": "Hello Ember",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "authors": ["Your Name"],
  "capabilities": ["runtime"],
  "dependencies": []
}
</pre>

The <code>id</code> is the unique package identifier. The <code>name</code> is shown to players. The <code>version</code> follows the package's release version. <code>authors</code> identifies the creators. <code>capabilities</code> lists the supported actions the mod requests. <code>dependencies</code> lists other mods required by this package.

The [https://bonsaibauer.github.io/shroudforge/schemas/manifest.schema.json canonical manifest schema] defines the accepted fields and data types.

